    <h2>Part 5: QA Self-Verification Phases</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>DSP UI Binding:</strong> VU-Meter/Spectrum respond fluidly to 16 telemetry floats
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Haptics:</strong> Short, snappy impulses only (<code>KEYBOARD_TAP</code>/<code
          >CONFIRM</code
        >)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Performance:</strong> No jank (Logcat: "Choreographer: Skipped frames" = Fail)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Layout &amp; Routing:</strong> Glassmorphism/Adaptive Transparency, clear data hierarchy
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Hard Rules</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Always concrete Hz/dB/ms/Ratio — no generics</li>
      <li>No allocation noise in the recomposition loop; no allocations in RT audio path</li>
      <li>CPU shedding threshold: 92% utilization → reduce self-load</li>
      <li>Architecture inviolable: UI → JNI Bridge → C++ (no bypass)</li>
      <li>Every AI action is undoable (undo mandatory)</li>
      <li>
        Mobile reality: Export, inference, and visualizers compete for resources — priority always
        Live Audio
      </li>
    </ol>
